ent. Uniform derivative bounds refer to the original grouped coordinates.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-color-exclusion"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.color_exclusion","kind":"claim","label":"Raw seed reencoding and ancestor exclusion","locator":"03-classical-optimization.tex:339–551; def:exclusion-formulas, eq:raw-seed-reencoding, lem:classical-color-exclusion","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","statement":"A single raw standard Gaussian is measurably recoded into an even finite color and an independent odd Gaussian seed; the induced rooted isometry intertwines L. For a fixed bounded odd smooth formula with bounded first derivatives, excluding current color, all path-ancestor colors and all helpers gives ‖f_col−f‖²≤C(α+p_H), where α is the largest nonhelper color probability and C depends on the fixed uncolored formula, not the number of colors. The output vanishes on helpers.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.color_exclusion","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","id":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22circuit.color_exclusion%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22circuit.color_exclusion%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.color_exclusion"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","id":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%2